# Reference papers — third-party copyrighted material, kept local only.
# See docs/SOURCES.md for the citation list.
docs/*.pdf
docs/*.docx
docs/*.epub

# OS / editor cruft
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
.DS_Store
*~
.vscode/
.idea/

# OneDrive / Office lock files
~$*
*.tmp

# Secrets — never commit real API keys. Copy harness/.env.harness.example to
# harness/.env.harness.local and fill that in; it is read by
# `node --env-file=harness/.env.harness.local`, not by git. The harness uses
# .env.harness rather than .env on purpose, so it can never collide with a
# project's own .env. No leading slash, so these match at every level,
# harness/ included.
.env
.envrc
.env.*

# One exception: the tracked, placeholders-only template. Nothing else is
# re-admitted — an .env.example someone fills in by mistake is how keys reach
# a commit.
!.env.harness.example

# Credentials and private keys, whatever they get named.
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa
id_ed25519
service-account*.json

# Runtime state a local rehearsal writes (which models have been seen before)
.agent/
node_modules/

# Local Claude Code agent definitions — steward this repo (code review,
# diagram alignment, doc/repo accuracy) but are personal tooling, not part
# of the portable harness this repository ships. Kept local, same as
# carrotgame's are project-local to that repo rather than this one.
.claude/agents/

# Kilo's worktrees — a full checkout of this repository per agent worktree,
# a few megabytes each. Excluded here rather than only in .git/info/exclude,
# which is local and does not travel with a clone.
.kilo/

# VS Code Local History extension — snapshots of files as they were edited,
# including copies of .claude/agents/ which is itself ignored above.
.history/

# Test-run output. `npm test` prints TAP to stdout; redirecting it to a file is
# a local debugging habit, not something a clone should carry.
*.tap
test-output*.txt
